{#- The "help me choose" email capture. Rendered twice per plan page — once
    beside the buy button, once in the help box at the foot — so it lives here
    rather than being copy-pasted.

    Expects `captureSource` (`buybox` | `helpbox`), used for the input id, the
    GA4 event and the payload so the two placements can be told apart in
    reporting. Without it both instances would emit identical `generate_lead`
    events and there'd be no way to know which one people actually use.

    Status strings come through data-* attributes rather than being hardcoded
    in plan-capture.js — the JS carried its own copy of them, which silently
    contradicted planUi.json the moment the copy changed (it was still promising
    "we sent it to you" after the offer became "we'll help you choose"). One
    source of truth: planUi.json. -#}
<form class="plan-capture-form"
      data-plan-id="{{ plan.id }}"
      data-plan-name="{{ plan.displayName | escape }}"
      data-lang="{{ lang }}"
      data-source="{{ captureSource }}"
      data-page-url="{{ page.url | absoluteUrl }}"
      data-submitting="{{ u.captureSubmitting | escape }}"
      data-success="{{ u.captureSuccess | escape }}"
      data-error="{{ u.captureError | escape }}">
  <div class="plan-capture-row">
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="pc-{{ captureSource }}-{{ plan.id }}">{{ u.captureEmailLabel }}</label>
    <input type="email" id="pc-{{ captureSource }}-{{ plan.id }}" name="email"
           placeholder="{{ u.capturePlaceholder }}" required>
    <button type="submit">{{ u.captureSubmit }}</button>
  </div>
  <p class="plan-capture-status"></p>
</form>
